{
  "id": "infinitiv-mit-zu",
  "name": "Present subjunctive: the forms (hable, coma, tenga, vaya)",
  "level": "B1",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "es419": { "note": "The forms are the same in Latin America, without vosotros (habléis, comáis): ustedes hablen, ustedes coman." },
  "subtitle": "The present subjunctive swaps the vowel: -ar verbs take -e endings (hable), -er and -ir verbs take -a endings (coma, viva). Most irregular forms come from the yo form of the present: tengo → tenga, hago → haga. You will usually see it after que: Quiero que vengas.",
  "briefMarks": ["hable", "coma", "viva", "tenga", "haga", "dé", "esté", "haya", "vaya", "sepa", "sea"],
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-b1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "quiero que · espero que · necesito que", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "hable · coma · viva · tenga · vaya", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">Quiero que</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">hables</span> con el casero. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Espero que</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">comas</span> bien. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Necesito que</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">vengas</span> mañana. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Espero que</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">sea</span> fácil.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>The vowel swaps.</strong> <em>-ar</em> verbs take <em>e</em>: <em>hable, hables, hable, hablemos, habléis, hablen</em>. <em>-er</em> and <em>-ir</em> verbs take <em>a</em>: <em>coma, comas, coma, comamos, comáis, coman</em>; <em>viva, vivas, viva, vivamos, viváis, vivan</em>.",
        "tag": "Regular"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>yo</strong> and <strong>él, ella, usted</strong> have the same form: <em>Quiere que yo hable. Quiero que ella hable.</em> The rest of the sentence tells you who it is.",
        "tag": "Same form"
      },
      {
        "html": "Start from the <strong>yo form of the present</strong>, drop <em>-o</em>, add the ending: <em>tengo → tenga, hago → haga, digo → diga, pongo → ponga, salgo → salga, vengo → venga, conozco → conozca</em>. This works for every person: <em>tengas, tengamos, tengáis</em>.",
        "tag": "From yo"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>Stem changes</strong> stay as in the present: <em>piense, vuelva</em>. With <em>nosotros</em> and <em>vosotros</em>, <em>-ar</em> and <em>-er</em> verbs go back to the plain stem: <em>pensemos, volvamos</em>. <em>-ir</em> verbs keep a small change: <em>duerma → durmamos, pida → pidamos</em>.",
        "tag": "Stem changes"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>Spelling</strong> keeps the sound: <em>buscar → busque, llegar → llegue, pagar → pague, empezar → empiece, coger → coja</em>.",
        "tag": "Spelling"
      },
      {
        "html": "Six verbs don't follow the yo rule. Learn them by heart: <em>dar → dé, estar → esté, haber → haya, ir → vaya, saber → sepa, ser → sea</em>. <em>dé</em> has an accent to tell it apart from the word <em>de</em>; <em>esté</em> has one because the stress falls on the last syllable.",
        "tag": "Six to learn"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Quiero que tienes</em> → ✓ <em>Quiero que tengas</em>. ✗ <em>Espero que hablas</em> → ✓ <em>Espero que hables</em>. ✗ <em>que yo sabe</em> → ✓ <em>que yo sepa</em>. ✗ <em>que dormamos</em> → ✓ <em>que durmamos</em>. When to use the subjunctive comes in the next topics; here, learn the forms.",
    "reference": {
